        <h2 class="cc-section-title">Where DTF earns its slot</h2>
        <p class="cc-section-body">And where Cricut, sublimation, and HTV still win. You've already invested in your craft. This isn't about switching. It's about knowing when to add another tool.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="cc-method-grid">

        <div class="cc-method-card">
          <div class="cc-method-card-top">
            <h3 class="cc-method-name">DTF Transfers</h3>
            <span class="cc-method-badge cc-badge-dtf">DTF</span>
          </div>
          <p class="cc-method-wins-label">When this earns its slot</p>
          <p class="cc-method-wins">Bulk orders of 50 shirts or more. Designs with gradients, photo-real detail, or a lot of colors on a dark fabric. No-minimum test prints when you're prototyping a new design and don't want to set up your press for three shirts.</p>
          <a href="{{ url_dtf }}" class="cc-method-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener">DTF transfers at Ninja ↗</a>
        </div>

        <div class="cc-method-card">
          <div class="cc-method-card-top">
            <h3 class="cc-method-name">Sublimation</h3>
            <span class="cc-method-badge cc-badge-sub">Sublimation</span>
          </div>
          <p class="cc-method-wins-label">When this earns its slot</p>
          <p class="cc-method-wins">Polyester blanks, all-over prints, and photo-quality work on light or white fabric. If the fabric is at least 65% poly, sublimation is cleaner. If it's cotton, you'll need a different path.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="cc-method-card">
          <div class="cc-method-card-top">
            <h3 class="cc-method-name">Vinyl / HTV</h3>
            <span class="cc-method-badge cc-badge-vinyl">Vinyl</span>
          </div>
          <p class="cc-method-wins-label">When this earns its slot</p>
          <p class="cc-method-wins">One-off custom jobs, single-color names and numbers, small quantity quick turns. If a client wants three personalized shirts by Thursday, HTV is still your friend. Don't overcomplicate it.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="cc-method-card">
